            'text-xs text-gray-500">cPanel Linux deployment flow from clean OS to WHM access.</figcaption></figure>\n'
            '  <p>Before initiating the installation script, verify that your server meets the official baseline '
            'requirements:</p>\n'
            '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
            '    <li><strong>Supported Operating System:</strong> AlmaLinux 8/9, Rocky Linux 8/9, CloudLinux 8/9, or '
            'Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (Minimal install recommended).</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Hardware:</strong> Minimum 2 GB RAM (4 GB+ strongly recommended for production), 1.1 GHz '
            'CPU, and at least 20 GB disk space (40 GB+ recommended).</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Networking:</strong> A dedicated, static public IPv4 address (cPanel does not support '
            'dynamic DHCP addresses or NAT-only servers without proper 1:1 public routing).</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Clean System:</strong> Zero pre-existing web server, mail, or database packages.</li>\n'
            '  </ul>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 1: Set a Fully Qualified '
            'Domain Name (FQDN) Hostname</h2>\n'
            '  <p>cPanel requires a valid FQDN hostname that does not match any domain you plan to host as a customer '
            'account. Connect via SSH as <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
            'text-navy">root</code> and set the hostname:</p>\n'
            '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
            'text-gray-100"><code>hostnamectl set-hostname server1.yourdomain.com</code></pre>\n'
            '  <p>Create a matching DNS <code class="rounded bg-navy/80 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs text-amber-300">A '
            'Record</code> pointing <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
            'text-navy">server1.yourdomain.com</code> to your server\'s public IP address at your DNS registrar or '
            'Cloudflare.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 2: Update System Packages and '
            'Install Utilities</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Ensure all operating system libraries are current and install essential network utilities:</p>\n'
            '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># On '
            'AlmaLinux / Rocky Linux / CloudLinux:\n'
            'dnf update -y\n'
            'dnf install -y perl curl wget screen tmux\n'
            '\n'
            '# On Ubuntu:\n'
            'apt update && apt upgrade -y\n'
