            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">When switching makes sense</h2>\n'
            '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
            '    <li>You host many WordPress or WooCommerce sites and want server-level caching.</li>\n'
            '    <li>Your servers hit memory limits during traffic spikes.</li>\n'
            '    <li>You run <a href="/cpanel-license" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">cPanel</a> and '
            'want to keep your current vhost and <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
            'text-navy">.htaccess</code> setup.</li>\n'
            '  </ul>\n'
            '  <p>If your sites are low-traffic, or you need Apache-only modules, staying on Apache is reasonable. '
            'Test first on a staging server, keep a rollback plan, and confirm your add-ons, such as <a '
            'href="/cloudlinux-license" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">CloudLinux</a>, work with '
            'your setup.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Running LiteSpeed on cPanel '
            'servers</h2>\n'
            '  <p>On cPanel servers, LiteSpeed is installed and managed through a WHM plugin. It reads the Apache '
            'configuration that cPanel already generates, so accounts, domains and <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 '
            'py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">.htaccess</code> files keep working while the web server changes '
            "underneath. Like cPanel, the LiteSpeed license is bound to the server's public IP, so set up the license "
            'for that address before you switch. If you use CloudLinux, check the current compatibility notes for your '
            'versions.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Checklist before you switch</h2>\n'
            '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
            '    <li>Copy your current Apache configuration and note the modules you use.</li>\n'
            '    <li>Test a few busy sites on a staging server and compare memory and response times.</li>\n'
            '    <li>Confirm your control panel, security and backup tools work with LiteSpeed.</li>\n'
            '    <li>Schedule the change for a quiet period and keep a way to roll back.</li>\n'
            '  </ul>\n'
            '</section>\n',
