            '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">LiteSpeed Web Server (LSWS) is the gold standard for accelerating '
            'high-traffic WordPress, WooCommerce, and dynamic PHP websites on cPanel &amp; WHM servers. As a direct '
            'drop-in replacement for Apache, LiteSpeed reads existing <code>.htaccess</code> and mod_rewrite '
            'directives natively while serving concurrent requests with an event-driven architecture. This tutorial '
            'covers installing LiteSpeed on cPanel, compiling matching PHP modules, tuning worker threads, and '
            'configuring enterprise caching.</p>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Prerequisites and License '
            'Binding</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Before installing LiteSpeed, ensure your server meets the basic requirements:</p>\n'
            '  <figure class="my-2"><img src="/assets/img/blog/install-litespeed-on-cpanel-1.svg" alt="LiteSpeed Web '
            'Server deployment flow on cPanel and WHM" width="960" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async" '
            'class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200" /><figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-xs '
            'text-gray-500">LiteSpeed deployment steps: WHM plugin install, LSWS build, 1-click switch, and LSCache '
            'setup.</figcaption></figure>\n'
            '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
            '    <li>A running cPanel &amp; WHM installation on AlmaLinux 8/9, Rocky Linux, or Ubuntu 22.04.</li>\n'
            '    <li>An active <a href="/litespeed-license" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">LiteSpeed '
            'license</a> bound to your server public IPv4 address.</li>\n'
            '    <li>Root SSH access to the cPanel server.</li>\n'
            '    <li>Port UDP 443 open in your firewall for HTTP/3 QUIC acceleration.</li>\n'
            '  </ul>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 1: Installing the LiteSpeed '
            'WHM Plugin</h2>\n'
            '  <p>SSH into your cPanel server as root and execute the official LiteSpeed WHM plugin installation '
            'script:</p>\n'
            '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code>cd '
            '/usr/src\n'
            'wget https://www.litespeedtech.com/packages/cpanel/lsws_whm_plugin_install.sh\n'
            'chmod 755 lsws_whm_plugin_install.sh\n'
            './lsws_whm_plugin_install.sh\n'
            'rm -f lsws_whm_plugin_install.sh</code></pre>\n'
            '  <p>Once completed, log into your WHM dashboard and search for <strong>LiteSpeed Web Server '
            'Plugin</strong> under the Plugins section.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 2: Installing LiteSpeed Web '
            'Server via WHM</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Inside the LiteSpeed WHM Plugin interface:</p>\n'
            '  <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6 text-gray-700">\n'
            '    <li>Click <strong>Install LiteSpeed Web Server</strong>.</li>\n'
            '    <li>Select <em>I agree to the license agreement</em> and choose your license source (LicenBase '
            'automated IP license).</li>\n'
            '    <li>Set port offset to <code>0</code> for direct replacement, or <code>2000</code> if you wish to '
            'test on alternate ports first.</li>\n'
            '    <li>Enter your administrator email address and proceed with the installation.</li>\n'
            '  </ol>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 3: Building Matching PHP '
            '(lsphp) Modules</h2>\n'
            '  <p>To ensure all existing PHP extensions match your EasyApache 4 profile, click <strong>Build Matching '
            'PHP</strong> inside the LiteSpeed plugin. The compiler matches all installed PHP modules (GD, cURL, '
            'imagick, ionCube) into optimized <code>lsphp</code> binaries automatically.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 4: Switching from Apache to '
            'LiteSpeed</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Once PHP compilation completes:</p>\n'
            '  <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6 text-gray-700">\n'
            '    <li>Click <strong>Switch to LiteSpeed</strong> in the WHM plugin.</li>\n'
            '    <li>LiteSpeed immediately takes over ports 80 and 443 with zero downtime or service '
            'interruption.</li>\n'
            '    <li>Verify HTTP/3 QUIC support and fast response times across your hosted domains.</li>\n'
            '  </ol>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 5: Mass Deploying the '
            'WordPress LSCache Plugin</h2>\n'
            '  <p>The standout feature of LiteSpeed is its server-level caching engine. In the WHM plugin, open the '
            '<strong>LiteSpeed Web Cache Manager</strong>:</p>\n'
            '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
            '    <li>Click <strong>WordPress Cache</strong> and run a server-wide scan.</li>\n'
            '    <li>Click <strong>Enable for All</strong> to inject and activate the LSCache plugin across all tenant '
            'WordPress installations automatically.</li>\n'
            '  </ul>\n'
            '  <p>Stack LiteSpeed with an authentic <a href="/cpanel-license" class="font-semibold text-brand '
            'hover:underline">cPanel license</a> and <a href="/wp-squared-license" class="font-semibold text-brand '
            'hover:underline">WP Squared</a> for unmatched WordPress hosting speed.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Fine-Tuning Worker Processes and '
            'Memory Limits</h2>\n'
            '  <p>For maximum server stability during heavy traffic spikes, adjust the external application process '
            'limits in the LiteSpeed WebAdmin Console (port 7080):</p>\n'
            '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
            '    <li><strong>Max Connections:</strong> Increase from 500 to 2000 to handle high concurrency.</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Memory Soft/Hard Limits:</strong> Increase memory ceiling per PHP worker from 400M to '
            '1024M for memory-intensive WooCommerce checkouts.</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Keep-Alive Timeout:</strong> Lower to 5 seconds to free idle TCP connections '
            'quickly.</li>\n'
            '  </ul>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Configuring Object Caching with '
            'Redis</h2>\n'
            '  <p>For dynamic database caching on high-traffic WooCommerce and forum communities, pair LiteSpeed with '
            'a localized Redis service:</p>\n'
            '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code>dnf '
            'install -y redis &amp;&amp; systemctl enable --now redis</code></pre>\n'
            '  <p>Enable the Redis Object Cache integration directly inside the WordPress LSCache settings under '
            '<em>Cache > [6] Object</em>, pointing to <code>127.0.0.1:6379</code>. This reduces database query load by '
            'up to 90%.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Verifying HTTP/3 QUIC and Cache '
            'Headers</h2>\n'
            '  <p>To confirm LiteSpeed is serving traffic with full caching and QUIC acceleration, run a cURL check '
            'against any hosted domain:</p>\n'
            '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code>curl -I '
            'https://yourdomain.com</code></pre>\n'
            '  <p>Look for the <code>server: LiteSpeed</code> and <code>x-litespeed-cache: hit</code> response '
            'headers. If present, your server is operating at peak performance.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n',
