            '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">Deploying a new Linux Virtual Private Server (VPS) takes only seconds, '
            'but deploying websites on an unhardened server invites immediate brute-force scans, malware injection, '
            'and unauthorized intrusion. Before configuring domains or installing a control panel, executing a '
            'systematic security hardening routine is mandatory. Here is the essential step-by-step security checklist '
            'for any production Linux VPS.</p>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">1. SSH Hardening: Keys and '
            'Non-Default Ports</h2>\n'
            '  <p>SSH is the primary target of automated credential stuffing. Harden SSH configuration in '
            '<code>/etc/ssh/sshd_config</code>:</p>\n'
            '  <figure class="my-2"><img src="/assets/img/blog/secure-linux-vps-hosting-websites-1.svg" alt="Linux VPS '
            'hardening and multi-layer security stack" width="960" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async" '
            'class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200" /><figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-xs '
            'text-gray-500">Multi-layer security architecture: SSH hardening, firewalls, kernel isolation, and AI '
            'WAF.</figcaption></figure>\n'
            '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
            '    <li><strong>Create a Sudo User:</strong> Create a non-root administrator account: <code>adduser '
            'adminuser &amp;&amp; usermod -aG wheel adminuser</code>.</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Deploy Ed25519 SSH Keys:</strong> Copy your public key to '
            '<code>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</code> and disable password login.</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Disable Root Password Login:</strong> Set <code>PermitRootLogin prohibit-password</code> '
            'and <code>PasswordAuthentication no</code>.</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Change the SSH Port:</strong> Change port 22 to a custom high port (e.g. <code>Port '
            '22220</code>) to filter 99% of automated mass scanners.</li>\n'
            '  </ul>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">2. Firewall and Intrusion '
            'Prevention</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Never expose unneeded ports to the public internet. Deploy a robust firewall and intrusion '
            'prevention system:</p>\n'
            '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
            '    <li><strong>Configure UFW or CSF:</strong> Restrict open inbound ports strictly to HTTP (80), HTTPS '
