            '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">Deploying cPanel &amp; WHM on a Virtual Private Server transforms a raw '
            'Linux virtual machine into a fully automated web hosting platform. However, because cPanel installs '
            'customized Apache, MySQL, PHP, and mail servers at the root system level, strict adherence to '
            'prerequisites and installation procedures is required. This step-by-step tutorial walks you through '
            'prerequisites, automated script execution, license activation, and post-installation tuning.</p>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">cPanel VPS Installation Pipeline '
            'Overview</h2>\n'
            '  <p>The installation workflow consists of three primary phases: preparing the base operating system, '
            'executing the automated cPanel installer, and verifying software licenses and initial WHM '
            'configurations.</p>\n'
            '  <figure class="my-2"><img src="/assets/img/blog/how-to-install-cpanel-on-vps-1.svg" alt="Step-by-step '
            'pipeline for installing cPanel and WHM on a Linux VPS server" width="960" height="420" loading="lazy" '
            'decoding="async" class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200" /><figcaption class="mt-2 text-center '
            'text-xs text-gray-500">End-to-end installation pipeline for cPanel & WHM on a Linux virtual '
            'machine.</figcaption></figure>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 1: Verify Hardware &amp; OS '
            'Prerequisites</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Before launching the installer, confirm that your VPS satisfies the official cPanel minimum hardware '
            'requirements:</p>\n'
            '  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
            '    <li><strong>CPU &amp; Memory:</strong> Minimum 1 vCPU and 2 GB RAM (4 GB RAM recommended for '
            'multi-site hosting).</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Disk Space:</strong> Minimum 20 GB of free storage (40 GB+ NVMe SSD recommended).</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Operating System:</strong> Clean, minimal install of AlmaLinux 8 or 9, Rocky Linux 8 or '
            '9, or Ubuntu 22.04 LTS.</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Static Public IP:</strong> A dedicated, publicly reachable IPv4 address with valid '
            'reverse DNS (PTR).</li>\n'
            '    <li><strong>Fully Qualified Domain Name (FQDN):</strong> Set a valid hostname such as <code '
            'class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">server1.yourdomain.com</code>.</li>\n'
            '  </ul>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 2: Prepare the Base Operating '
            'System</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Log in to your VPS via SSH as the root user and execute the following preparatory commands to '
            'disable OS firewalls during setup, update packages, and set your server hostname:</p>\n'
            '  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><pre><code># '
            '1. Update system packages\n'
            'dnf update -y\n'
            '\n'
            '# 2. Set the Fully Qualified Domain Name (FQDN) hostname\n'
            'hostnamectl set-hostname server1.yourdomain.com\n'
            '\n'
            '# 3. Disable OS default firewalld to prevent port blocks during setup\n'
            'systemctl stop firewalld\n'
            'systemctl disable firewalld\n'
            '\n'
            '# 4. Install screen or tmux to prevent SSH session disconnects\n'
            'dnf install screen perl curl wget -y</code></pre></div>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Step 3: Run the Official cPanel '
            '&amp; WHM Installer</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Launch a screen session and execute the official cPanel installation script. Screen ensures that if '
            'your SSH connection drops, the installation continues unhindered in the background:</p>\n'
            '  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><pre><code># '
            'Start a persistent screen session\n'
            'screen -S cpanel-install\n'
            '\n'
            '# Download and run the automated installation script\n'
            'cd /home &amp;&amp; curl -o latest -L https://securedownloads.cpanel.net/latest &amp;&amp; sh '
            'latest</code></pre></div>\n'
            '  <p>The installer will automatically download, compile, and configure the cPanel core binaries, Perl '
            'dependencies, Apache web server, and database daemons. This process usually completes within 20 to 45 '
