            '<p class="text-lg text-gray-600">Seeing a <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
            'text-navy">cPanel License Validation Failed</code> or <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 '
            'text-[0.85em] text-navy">Cannot Determine License Status</code> warning locks users out of WebHost '
            'Manager (WHM) and displays critical license renewal banners to client websites. License errors typically '
            'stem from network egress blocks, system clock drift, IP mismatch in NAT environments, or stale cached '
            'license files. Follow this comprehensive diagnostic guide to resolve cPanel license errors in '
            'minutes.</p>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">cPanel License Troubleshooting '
            'Workflow</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Diagnosing cPanel license validation failures follows a systematic multi-stage verification process: '
            'forcing sync commands, checking networking/clock synchronization, clearing corrupted tokens, and '
            'refreshing wholesale IP bindings.</p>\n'
            '  <figure class="my-2"><img src="/assets/img/blog/cpanel-license-not-working-fix-guide-1.svg" '
            'alt="Diagnostic troubleshooting workflow for resolving cPanel license activation and synchronization '
            'errors" width="960" height="420" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="w-full rounded-2xl border '
            'border-gray-200" /><figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-gray-500">Diagnostic workflow for '
            'resolving cPanel & WHM licensing errors.</figcaption></figure>\n'
            '  <p>Understanding these diagnostic stages ensures that you resolve license lockouts swiftly without '
            'unnecessary server reboots or service interruptions.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Fix 1: Run the Official cpkeyclt '
            'License Update Command</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Log in to your server via SSH as the root user and execute the cPanel key client utility:</p>\n'
            '  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
            'text-gray-100"><pre><code>/usr/local/cpanel/cpkeyclt</code></pre></div>\n'
            "  <p>If the license is active on your server's public IP address, the terminal will output <code "
            'class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">Updating cPanel license...Done. Update '
            'succeeded.</code></p>\n'
            '  <p>If the output returns a license check failure, verify that outbound traffic to <code class="rounded '
            'bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">auth.cpanel.net</code> on port 80 and 443 is permitted in '
            'your CSF/iptables firewall. Test connectivity with curl:</p>\n'
            '  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
            'text-gray-100"><pre><code>curl -Iv https://auth.cpanel.net</code></pre></div>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Fix 2: Synchronize System Clock '
            'Drift (NTP / Chrony)</h2>\n'
            '  <p>cPanel uses cryptographic timestamps to validate license tokens. If your server clock drifts by more '
            'than a few minutes from UTC, validation will fail automatically with an invalid certificate or timestamp '
            'error.</p>\n'
            '  <p>Synchronize your system clock via chrony or systemd-timesyncd:</p>\n'
            '  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><pre><code># '
            'On AlmaLinux / RHEL / Rocky Linux\n'
            'chronyc makestep\n'
            'systemctl restart chronyd\n'
            '\n'
            '# On Ubuntu / Debian\n'
            'timedatectl set-ntp on\n'
            'systemctl restart systemd-timesyncd</code></pre></div>\n'
            '  <p>Once system time is aligned with global UTC time servers, re-run <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 '
            'py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">/usr/local/cpanel/cpkeyclt</code> to complete the cryptographic '
            'validation handshake.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Fix 3: Resolve IP Mismatch &amp; '
            'NAT Routing Issues</h2>\n'
            '  <p>On cloud VPS providers (like AWS EC2, Google Cloud, or Azure), the internal private IP differs from '
            'your elastic public IP. Check which public IP your server is presenting to the licensing servers:</p>\n'
            '  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
            'text-gray-100"><pre><code>curl -s https://api.ipify.org</code></pre></div>\n'
            '  <p>Ensure that the IP returned by curl matches the exact IP registered on your <a '
            'href="/cpanel-license" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">cPanel license</a> order. If your '
            'server has multiple IP addresses and is routing outbound requests through an unassigned secondary '
            'interface, configure the default route or update <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
            'text-navy">/etc/sysconfig/network-scripts</code>.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Fix 4: Remove Corrupted License '
            'Cache Tokens</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Occasionally, an aborted update or power interruption can leave a stale or corrupted local license '
            "token file in cPanel's configuration directory. Resetting the local cached files forces the daemon to "
            'rebuild its cryptographic keyring:</p>\n'
            '  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><pre><code># '
            'Remove stale cached license file\n'
            'rm -f /usr/local/cpanel/cpanel.lisc\n'
            '\n'
            '# Re-run key client to fetch a fresh token\n'
            '/usr/local/cpanel/cpkeyclt\n'
            '\n'
            '# Restart cPanel services to apply changes\n'
            '/usr/local/cpanel/scripts/restartsrv_cpsrvd</code></pre></div>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Fix 5: Verify DNS Resolution for '
            'Licensing Gateways</h2>\n'
            '  <p>If your VPS cannot resolve the hostname <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
            'text-navy">auth.cpanel.net</code>, license updates will fail with DNS lookup errors. Verify your '
            'nameserver configuration in <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
            'text-navy">/etc/resolv.conf</code> and ensure reliable upstream resolvers are present:</p>\n'
            '  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed '
            'text-gray-100"><pre><code>nameserver 8.8.8.8\n'
            'nameserver 1.1.1.1</code></pre></div>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">Fix 6: LicenBase Automated '
            'Wholesale IP Sync</h2>\n'
            '  <p>If you are utilizing a wholesale automated IP license from LicenBase, run the one-step '
            'synchronization command provided in your client dashboard. Our gateway re-synchronizes your server IP '
            'address, clears stale local license tokens, and re-validates your server against the licensing network '
            'instantly.</p>\n'
            '  <p>In addition to cPanel, you can synchronize your <a href="/cloudlinux-license" class="font-semibold '
            'text-brand hover:underline">CloudLinux OS license</a> and <a href="/litespeed-license" '
            'class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">LiteSpeed Web Server</a> through our unified management '
            'platform.</p>\n'
            '  <p>Review our <a href="/deals" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">license bundle '
            'catalogue</a> or contact our 24/7 technical team via the <a href="/contact" class="font-semibold '
            'text-brand hover:underline">contact page</a> if you need assistance activating your server licenses.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n',
