            '8.8.8.8\n'
            "nameserver 1.1.1.1' > /etc/resolv.conf</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n"
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">2. Fix 1: Refreshing Local License '
            'Cache with cpkeyclt</h2>\n'
            '  <p>The primary tool for refreshing your cPanel license is <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 '
            'text-[0.85em] text-navy">cpkeyclt</code>. Execute this command as root via SSH:</p>\n'
            '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># '
            'Refresh license key client:\n'
            '/usr/local/cpanel/cpkeyclt\n'
            '\n'
            '# If successful, the terminal will output:\n'
            '# Updating cPanel license...Done. Update succeeded.</code></pre>\n'
            '  <p>If you are using a <a href="/cpanel-license" class="font-semibold text-brand '
            'hover:underline">LicenBase cPanel license</a>, running our wrapper command <code class="rounded bg-mist '
            'px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">licenbase_cpanel</code> performs both the authentication check and '
            'the local key update automatically.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">3. Fix 2: Verifying Server Public '
            'IPv4 Address</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Cloud instances on AWS, Google Cloud, or behind NAT firewalls often have internal private IPs (e.g. '
            '<code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] text-navy">10.0.0.5</code>) while broadcasting '
            'through an Elastic or Floating public IP. Confirm your outbound public IP:</p>\n'
            '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># Check '
            'actual outbound public IPv4:\n'
            'curl -4 icanhazip.com\n'
            '\n'
            '# Rebuild cPanel NAT mapping:\n'
            '/usr/local/cpanel/scripts/build_cpnat</code></pre>\n'
            '  <p>Ensure the IP returned by <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
            'text-navy">icanhazip.com</code> matches the IP registered in your LicenBase client dashboard.</p>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">4. Fix 3: Resolving Firewall and '
            'DNS Outbound Blocks</h2>\n'
            '  <p>If your ConfigServer Security &amp; Firewall (CSF) or iptables blocks outgoing connections on port '
            '80 or 443, your server cannot reach the licensing verification nodes. Test connectivity:</p>\n'
            '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># Test '
            'connectivity to verification cluster:\n'
            'curl -I https://verify.licenbase.com\n'
            '\n'
            '# If connection hangs, temporarily disable CSF to confirm:\n'
            'csf -x\n'
            '\n'
            '# If verification succeeds with CSF disabled, add outbound rules and re-enable:\n'
            'csf -e</code></pre>\n'
            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy">5. Fix 4: Synchronizing System '
            'Time and NTP Clocks</h2>\n'
            '  <p>Cryptographic license tokens require accurate server time stamps. If your server clock drifts by '
            'more than a few minutes, license validation requests will fail:</p>\n'
            '  <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-navy p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-100"><code># Force '
            'NTP clock synchronization on AlmaLinux / Rocky Linux:\n'
            'chronyc makestep\n'
            '\n'
            '# Check current time status:\n'
            'timedatectl</code></pre>\n'
            '  <p>After synchronizing the time, re-run <code class="rounded bg-mist px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.85em] '
            'text-navy">licenbase_cpanel</code> to reactivate WHM. For servers running high-traffic stacks, consider '
