            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4 tracking-tight">Deep Dive: CPU Worker Allocation '
            'and RAM Ceiling Mechanics</h2>\n'
            '  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">To make an informed decision when purchasing a LiteSpeed Web '
            "Server license, it is essential to understand how LiteSpeed's internal process manager enforces licensing "
            'constraints. In Apache, each worker process handles a single connection at a time. In contrast, LiteSpeed '
            'uses an event-driven architecture based on non-blocking I/O multiplexing. A single LiteSpeed worker '
            'process can handle thousands of concurrent HTTP and HTTPS transactions without creating additional '
            'operating system threads.</p>\n'
            '  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When a license specifies a 1-Worker limit (such as Starter, '
            'Site Owner, or Web Host Lite), the master process spawns exactly one active worker process. For '
            'high-traffic servers with heavy SSL handshakes and complex PHP execution loops, multi-worker tiers (Web '
