            '</section>\n'
            '\n'
            '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
            '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4 tracking-tight">The Technical Reality of '
            '.htaccess Processing: LiteSpeed vs Open-Source</h2>\n'
            '  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The single most important operational difference between '
            'LiteSpeed Enterprise and open-source alternatives like Nginx or OpenLiteSpeed is how configuration files '
            'are parsed in dynamic, multi-user hosting environments. In Apache, every HTTP request scans the directory '
            'tree for <code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-sm text-gray-800">.htaccess</code> files, '
            'causing high disk I/O and CPU overhead. Nginx solves this by eliminating <code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 '
            'py-0.5 rounded text-sm text-gray-800">.htaccess</code> entirely, but this breaks standard WordPress '
            'plugins and security rules unless every directive is manually converted into server blocks.</p>\n'
            '  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">LiteSpeed Enterprise delivers the best of both worlds: it '
